# W-B-Q1: schedule over a calendar whose added list holds a one_of window. L §4.2: a day in added may be a window,
# "every day known but one. Such a window is one the line meets, so a result that depends on its day is HOLE-IMPRECISE
# unless the line states windows each (§4.4)"; L §4.4: "Built-ins on a window ... give the interval of their values",
# "Only a comparison decides an interval", "One rule for every window a line meets ... a day in a calendar's added
# list (§4.2)"; L §5.14: `on d` is "a date, a window (§4.4), a hole, or none". pay[2026-06] is scheduled on Monday
# 2026-06-22, rolled following: where the added day is 06-22 it is 06-23, where it is 06-23 it is 06-22 (d2, windows
# each), so its day is the window of the two (d1), not a hole with no bound (L §5.14 bounds only "a day that is a hole
# and not a window"). L §4.4: "A movement dated by a window counts in a span when its whole window lies inside it, and
# not at all when it lies wholly outside. When it crosses an end of the span, flows over that span is a hole
# (HOLE-IMPRECISE), and so is bal(x, d) for a d inside the window": f6 and b1 count it, f5 doesn't, f6a and b2 are
# holes. The interval spans every day the window can take (one pass per day), not only its first and last
# (HANDOVER contradiction 46).
=== m.tally
model m
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
input len: calendar
input pay_dom: int
input amt: money PLN
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2019-05-01..
place employer: outside lives 1900-01-01..

move pay[m in months]: transfers
  on schedule(m, pay_dom, following, len)
  at start_of(m)
  leg cash from employer to konto amount amt

ask d1: schedule(2026-06, pay_dom, following, len) law 2026-06-01
ask d2: schedule(2026-06, pay_dom, following, len) law 2026-06-01 windows each
ask f5: flows(pay, 2026-05)
ask f6: flows(pay, 2026-06)
ask f6a: flows(pay, 2026-06-01..2026-06-22)
ask b1: bal(konto, 2026-06-30)
ask b2: bal(konto, 2026-06-22)

version v
  cite s
  governs 2026
  known 2025-12-01
  len = calendar(weekends [sat, sun], added [one_of([2026-06-22, 2026-06-23])])
  pay_dom = 22 "own"
  amt = 100.00 PLN "own"
  opening[konto] = 0.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "own"
=== expect
b1: 600.00 PLN
  unfulfilled: pay[2026-01]
  unfulfilled: pay[2026-02]
  unfulfilled: pay[2026-03]
  unfulfilled: pay[2026-04]
  unfulfilled: pay[2026-05]
  unfulfilled: pay[2026-06]
  cut 2026-12-31
b2: ?"date within window(2026-06-22, 2026-06-23) not precise enough for a balance" (pay[2026-06])
  unfulfilled: pay[2026-01]
  unfulfilled: pay[2026-02]
  unfulfilled: pay[2026-03]
  unfulfilled: pay[2026-04]
  unfulfilled: pay[2026-05]
  cut 2026-12-31
d1: window(2026-06-22, 2026-06-23)
  law date 2026-06-01, cut 2026-12-31
d2 [added one_of([2026-06-22, 2026-06-23]) = 2026-06-22]: 2026-06-23
  law date 2026-06-01, cut 2026-12-31
d2 [added one_of([2026-06-22, 2026-06-23]) = 2026-06-23]: 2026-06-22
  law date 2026-06-01, cut 2026-12-31
f5: 100.00 PLN
  unfulfilled: pay[2026-05]
  cut 2026-12-31
f6: 100.00 PLN
  unfulfilled: pay[2026-06]
  cut 2026-12-31
f6a: ?"date within window(2026-06-22, 2026-06-23) not precise enough for flows of pay" (pay[2026-06])
  cut 2026-12-31
